Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS — enable content editors to see real-time updates to Contentstack content within the application without requiring a full page reload, by integrating Contentstack's Live Preview capability into the existing content delivery pipeline.

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack client is initialized (line 69: contentstack.Stack(options)). The options object (lines 55-67) lacks the live_preview configuration required by Contentstack's Live Preview SDK. Without live_preview config here, no downstream component can receive real-time preview data — this is the root cause, not any presentation-layer component.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a live_preview property to the options object (lines 55-67), reading CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN from process.env (following the existing pattern on lines 17-24). The options object should include: live_preview: { enable: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW === 'true', preview_timestamp: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN }. Then after Stack creation (after line 72), call Stack.livePreview(options) per Contentstack Live Preview SDK docs. This enables the Stack to receive preview content — all 236+ callers of useContent will then be able to serve live-previewed data without any component-level changes.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is where content is provided to the entire React tree via context. After the Stack is configured for Live Preview on the server side, the client-side ContentstackProvider must integrate @contentstack/live-preview-utils to listen for real-time content edits and update the context value, enabling components to re-render with preview content without a full page reload.
  - **Minimal fix:** Import and initialize @contentstack/live-preview-utils (LivePreview) at module level with the same Stack config. Inside ContentstackProvider, replace the static useMemo with a useState+useEffect pattern: useState for content initialized from defaultContent, and useEffect that calls LivePreview.onEntryChange(callback) to update the content state whenever Contentstack emits a preview change. This makes the context reactive to live preview edits, propagating updates to all 236+ useContent consumers without page reload.


